[Term]
id: CL:0002071
name: enterocyte of epithelium of large intestine
def: "A columnar absorptive epithelial cell found in the epithelium of large intestine, specialized for water and electrolyte absorption. Unlike small intestinal enterocytes, those in the large intestine have fewer apical microvilli." [GOC:tfm, ISBN:0517223651, PMID:22288583, PMID:35626748, PMID:38872928]
