[Term]
id: CL:0002337
name: keratinocyte stem cell
def: "A stem cell found in the basal layer of the epidermis, hair follicle, and sebaceous gland, characterised by its quiescent nature, high proliferative potential, and capacity for long-term self-renewal. This cell maintains epidermal homeostasis by producing transit-amplifying cells that differentiate to replenish the stratified squamous epithelium." [PMID:15339667, PMID:20568222, PMID:9520465]
synonym: "KSC" RELATED OMO:0003000 [PMID:9520465]
